     The bbhhnndd__eerroomm__pprroobbee() function returns a standard DEVICE_PROBE(9) result.

     A return value equal to or less than zero indicates success.  Values
     greater than zero indicates an error, and will be an appropriate error
     code.  For values less than or equal to zero, the erom class returning
     the highest value should be used to parse the erom table.  ENXIO is re‐
     turned if the device is not supported by the parser.

